  "id": "COMPOUND:20538 - PROTEIN:4886",
  "verbalization": "Brandisianin C is implicated in the target pathway leading to Serine/threonine-protein kinase ATR through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Brandisianin C directly targets Disintegrin and metalloproteinase domain-containing protein 9, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including (1S)-1-methyl-4-propan-2-ylcyclohex-3-en-1-ol and 1-(5,7,8-Trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-2H-1-benzopyran-6-yl)ethanone. These compounds are all potential ligands for the same target, Serine/threonine-protein kinase ATR, indicating a shared mechanism of action. The presence of multiple pathways converging on ATR suggests that Brandisianin C may exert its effects through a common intermediate, possibly by modulating the activity of Disintegrin and metalloproteinase domain-containing protein 9. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of this kinase in the biological response to Brandisianin C, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
